  "name": "nanosecond-pulsed-laser-ablation-as-a-universal-method-for-oxide-removal",
  "notes": "This dataset contains all relevant files for the publication: \"Nanosecond-Pulsed Laser Ablation as a Universal  Method for Oxide Removal and Surface Structuring of Aluminum and Copper for Advanced Manufacturing Applications\"\r\n\r\n# Dataset description\r\nThe Data is available in the original processing formats.\r\n\r\n## CLSM - Roughness measurements\r\n- CLSM-Data of aluminum and copper samples in .vk6-Format  \r\n- Exported Pictures  \r\n- Excel-Files of exported roughness values (Sa, Sq, Sz, Sp, Sv, Sal, Sdq, Sdr, Std, Str, Spd, Spc)\r\n- Python-Scripts for Plotting\r\n\r\n## Nanoindentation\r\n- Excel-Files of Nanoindentation measurements\r\n- Python-Script for Plotting\r\n\r\n## XRD\r\n- Residual Stresses: Raw-Data from XRD-Measurements on aluminum and copper samples\r\n- Texture: Raw-Data from XRD-Measurements on aluminum and copper samples\r\n- Python-Script for Plotting\r\n\r\n## XPS\r\n- Raw-Data and Plots of XPS measurements of aluminum and copper samples\r\n\r\n## Data from the Section 'Applications in Manufacturing'\r\nData used to generate plots in the application-section of the paper with the following manufacturing processes:  \r\n\r\n* Adhesive bonding  \r\n- Cold roll bonding  \r\n- Compound casting  \r\n- Laser beam brazing  \r\n\r\n\r\n# Citation\r\nJanthur, Finn-Lennard and Seffer, Sarah and Hermsdorf, Jörg and Barienti, Khemais and Heimers, Henri and Steinhoff, Timon and Nürnberger, Florian and Klose, Christian and Herbst, Sebastian and Maier, Hans Jürgen and Kuhr, Lara and Raumel, Selina and Wurz, Marc and Gerland, Sandra and Raatz, Annika and Zimmermann, Sascha and Bürger, Friedrich and Gustus, René and Maus-Friedrichs, Wolfgang and Overmeyer, Ludger, \"Nanosecond-Pulsed Laser Ablation as a Universal Method for Oxide Removal and Surface Structuring of Aluminum and Copper for Advanced Manufacturing Applications\", vol. 34, pp. 101018, https://doi.org/10.1016/j.apsadv.2026.101018\r\n\r\n\r\n# Funding\r\nFunded by the Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft (DFG, German Research Foundation) – Project-ID 394563137 – SFB 1368.  \r\nOpen access funding enabled and organized by Projekt DEAL.\r\n",
